      "id": "full",
      "type": "cv.fourier_components",
      "name": "Fourier magnitude and phase components",
      "documentation": "<p>Phase-only uses F/|F| where phase exceeds both floors, and zero elsewhere. Magnitude-only uses |F| + 0i. Full retains both components. DC removal precedes thresholding. Outputs retain conjugate symmetry for a real inverse.</p><p>The typed spectrum requests floating inverse output. Magnitude-only receives a new spatial frame; it has no source-position mapping. Diagnostic images are frequency-bin grids, with invalid phase values zero and a separate validity mask.</p><p><a href=\"https://docs.opencv.org/5.0/main_modules/core_array.html\">OpenCV DFT reference</a>.</p>",
      "parameters": {
        "components": "full",
        "dc": "keep",
        "relative_floor": 1e-06,
        "absolute_floor": 0.0,
        "symmetry": "require",
        "precision": "auto",
        "layout": "centered"
      },
